// The C ABI exports of the test world (decisions 0204, 0207; the zero-C
// audit's B14): like cabi.xo, every top level function here is called
// by the C runtime as xo_x_<name>. The SSA builders build them in test
// binaries only (selfhost/ssa build.xo declare_exports); the C calls
// them only in the test world (tw.on), and has weak definitions for the
// programs without them (std/llrt/xo_rt.c, the test world). The state is
// testworld.xo's and twrun.xo's.
use native/llrt/twrun

/// Starts the test world (entry.xo's E_TW_INIT word).
fn tw_start() { twrun.start() }

/// Releases the values the test world keeps, at the end of the test (C
/// main, after main's thread).
fn tw_end() { twrun.end() }

/// Moves the virtual clock after a deadlock check (xo_rt.c
/// xo_sched_rt's op 2, while the clock is virtual).
fn tw_kick() { twrun.kick() }

// Part 2 (std/native/llrt/twrun.xo, the zero-C audit's B15)

/// A sleep for FakeClock.sleeps (xo_rt.c clock_wait).
fn tw_sleep(d: Int) { twrun.sleep_record(d) }
